# Authors: Simon Davidson & Claude | Created 2026-08-19 | Last modified 2026-08-19
#
# tb_config_manager at the REAL deployed config width (WORDS_PER_CONFIG=16, as
# instantiated by flexman.v, fmi_top.v, example_app_top.v and a deployment top),
# with the default latency-agnostic config engine and a COMBINATIONAL cfg
# memory model.
#
# This is the build the config-push latency check actually bites on: at the
# tb's default WPC=4 the untouched 4-send BBA engine sets the latency, so the
# config engine's stride is invisible. Expects 34 cycles (was 49 before the
# read of word w+1 was overlapped with the accelerator write of word w).
xrun -sv -timescale 10ps/1ps -access wrc -top tb_config_manager \
  -define WPC16 \
  config_manager.v tb_config_manager.v
